  id: Pulmonary_artery1
  partName: Pulmonary Artery
  descriptionChunks:
  - The pulmonary arteries carry deoxygenated blood from the heart to the lungs for
    oxygenation. They originate from the right ventricle and branch into left and
    right pathways.
  - This circulation is essential for gas exchange, allowing carbon dioxide to be
    removed and oxygen to be absorbed. Proper function of these arteries is critical
    for maintaining respiratory efficiency and ensuring that oxygenated blood is
    returned to the heart for distribution.
